One notification per record, in browsers and on iPhone.

Base: zan-workspace main at e0d71b9.
Apply from the web repo root:
    git apply --check one-notification-per-record.patch
    git apply one-notification-per-record.patch

What it changes:
- The service worker tags each push about a record with its channel and entityId. A new update
  replaces the last one and alerts again, as on Android. A push with no record, such as the test
  push, stays as it is.
- A callback push stays on screen until someone acts on it (requireInteraction). Nothing sends a
  callback push yet.
- sendPush adds apns-collapse-id, so an iPhone replaces the last update too. It does nothing until
  the iOS app exists.

No action buttons in the browser: a click already opens the record, and Android's guide says a
button must not repeat what a tap does.

Browsers read title, body and url as before. No migration and no new environment variable.

